<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Dogs mate (Continued) (Mlie.DogsMate, Workshop 2441132298, after Revolus' original).

  That mod lets animals of one group mate with each other. A group is a Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef whose
  pawnKinds list names the PawnKindDefs that may cross. It deduces nothing: an animal no group names cannot cross.

  The meffalo joins the group Bison, where the mod already puts the muffalo (1.6/Defs/CompatibleSpecies/Mammalia.xml,
  read 2026-10-11): the meffalo is a muffalo subspecies, so it follows its analogue.

  The boomsloth joins the group Boomalope, which holds only the boomalope. There is no group for the megasloth
  or any sloth in the mod, so no megasloth pairing can be declared here; the boomalope is the one parent that has
  a group. This agrees with the Better Crossbreeding patch, which pairs the boomsloth with the boomalope too.

  Only applied when that mod is active; without it this file changes nothing and logs nothing.
  PatchOperationFindMod matches the mod's display name. No load order is asked: the patch adds list items to
  defs that the mod ships, and the game applies patches after every def is loaded.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Dogs mate (Continued)</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>/Defs/Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef[defName="Bison"]/pawnKinds</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>Meffalo</li>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>/Defs/Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef[defName="Boomalope"]/pawnKinds</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>Boomsloth</li>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
